<title>JAPAN: Japan July beef imports up 22.8 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July beef imports up 22.8 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in July were up 22.8 percent from a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p> Total	    74,567	49,826	60,739</p>
<p> Refrigerated   26,939	23,565	30,307</p>
<p> Frozen	   47,628	26,261	30,432</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     16,216	13,709	18,375</p>
<p>  U.S.	     9,965	 8,790	10,967</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    July 96     June 96	July 95</p>
<p> U.S.	     28,727	13,728	10,967</p>
<p> Australia	15,632	 9,505	18,385</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first seven months of 1996 were 194,112 tonnes against 201,416 tonnes during the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the first seven months of 1996 came to 222,993 tonnes against 161,875 tonnes in the same period of 1995.</p>
</text>
